{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994621425210001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"woozy-gland-garb","assignee":"","author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":8},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Iso Tester","body":"FORCE_CLAIM: plan-review gate bypassed by user approval — no plan-review attestation was verified. Reason: \"Post-epic remediation (audit follow-on); implementing now.\".","timestamp":1782563012109979001}],"created_at":1782560954074383001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b6b7702c-46bd-4ab4-9a8a-6085322f5424","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1f19-adf2-ffb2-4b09"}],"description":"## What\nThe snapshot re-rooting is currently an UNGUARDED CONVENTION: there is no import-linter contract, gate registry, or test that fails CI when a new tool-using agent op reads cfg.repo_path / builds LLMConfig.from_env without going through gate_source. The run_workflow bypass proves the gap.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A CI-enforced guard fails when a new code path runs a tool-using agent (get_runner().run with filesystem_tools) without the gate snapshot process (e.g. an enumerated gate registry the surfaces test + a coverage test assert against, or an import-linter/AST contract on from_env/repo_path use, or a runtime assertion).\n- [ ] The guard catches the run_workflow class of bypass (or that path is whitelisted only with an explicit safe mechanism).\n- [ ] Documented in docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md: how to add a new agent op so it follows the process.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"gate_session + assert_gated guard"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"fail-closed at agent tool wiring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py","reason":"gate_read_root enters session"},{"path":"docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md","reason":"how-to add a new agent op"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_agent_op_safeguard.py","reason":"tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4c5ec822-f987-4258-9d78-a0b0eea645e8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d6cc-e0f2-75a1-4875","ticket_type":"task","title":"Safeguard: prevent new agentic operations from bypassing the snapshot process","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["af39dbda-3d63-4a0c-a080-01a20c0c4b4a","b6b7702c-46bd-4ab4-9a8a-6085322f5424","7dd54c66-0928-423e-946e-9824e29a5bda","4c5ec822-f987-4258-9d78-a0b0eea645e8","ce8eab33-14e4-408d-8c6f-4ac3008d777e","22df85f3-e26b-49b8-b399-891f0611a7d7","dbabea30-0024-4f7b-b8c3-fa0f7ec2cdb5","9371fec0-e46e-4ae2-8537-f1a5fa783afc"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994621425210001,"uuid":"3f9ebad4-1ee2-4b41-88a9-3963ee5c74e5"}